WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.614
The screen is four windows: left, center, right, and bottom.

2
00:00:04.614 --> 00:00:07.420
Each one holds tabs, like a desktop editor.

3
00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:10.498
The tab strip names what each window shows.

4
00:00:10.498 --> 00:00:14.529
Here: the Controls, the Renderer, the Patch Bay, and the Timeline.

5
00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:17.963
The arrow button in a window's corner maximizes it.

6
00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:19.483
Click it again to restore.

7
00:00:19.942 --> 00:00:23.571
The minus button collapses a window down to just its tab strip.

8
00:00:23.571 --> 00:00:26.683
Click the strip, or the same button, to bring it back.

9
00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:29.423
The Window menu has layout presets.

10
00:00:29.423 --> 00:00:31.964
Tall stacks everything into one column.

11
00:00:32.415 --> 00:00:34.591
Default brings back the four-window layout.

12
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.092
Under View, pick a skin.

13
00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:39.835
CRT is flat and compact.

14
00:00:39.835 --> 00:00:42.303
Hardware turns sliders into knobs.

15
00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:44.990
Rack, the default, adds patch cables.

16
00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:52.286
Control plus and Control minus change the text size.

17
00:00:52.286 --> 00:00:53.889
Control zero resets it.

18
00:00:54.347 --> 00:00:55.521
Rearrange freely.

19
00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:59.459
Reset Layout, in the Window menu, always brings you home.

20
00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.427
Next: sources.
